# Release-time demo artifacts. cmd/inspector/demo.tape renders the gif and the
# workflow cross-compiles a throwaway binary to record it; both are produced
# before goreleaser runs. Untracked, they put the tree in a dirty state and
# goreleaser aborts ("git is in a dirty state") — which is why every release
# from v0.0.10 onward failed and the repo has tags but no releases. The gif
# still reaches users: .goreleaser.yml attaches it via release.extra_files.
cmd/inspector/demo-bin
cmd/inspector/demo.gif
